   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "230cad6b-7900-e120-5133-453578bab00a"], Cell[
    "Logical error rate", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "086f7f71-a7b7-bd3e-3815-773ad2430404"], Cell["\<\
A closed-form binomial tail, and an independent sampled route\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"0cdf8892-1d3f-31f6-34e4-21dc94cb83dc"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "7e0217c2-6a7a-d359-2631-8eac0f0ca1a3"], Cell[
    "The extraction circuit", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "4104c6da-03d7-a765-773b-df84b6630a4f"], Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{"code", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Syndrome\>\"", ",", " ", "\[Ellipsis]"}], "]"}]], 
      "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "731f4b84-5335-8b87-2125-62ee66c1d9ed"],
     ", and the circuit run as a state on the engine"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"315717aa-70ab-e706-676c-8ef4015fca6c"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "7c1b1617-f81f-7a45-2438-8850f9aa48af"], Cell[
    "Detectors and faults", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "70b05f1a-470c-9c9d-2040-574472bee6e7"], Cell["\<\
Stim's own sampler, detector by detector, over two million shots\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"4a8c5b06-7c6a-07f5-7ab4-5360751f6ddf"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "4fa3f928-0446-c8dd-7550-f172adf09a27"], Cell[
    "Circuit-level rate", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "3727240c-f62b-7b8f-5edc-be6983de49d5"], Cell["\<\
The code-capacity polynomial it must reduce to, and a sampled route\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"50637aef-2122-41f7-0011-73c950d713dd"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "63773809-2d44-01f7-110c-b25344f153dd"], Cell[
    "Idle noise and the schedule", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "7ede8b7e-b317-5b7c-26e5-233bc6a22646"], Cell[TextData[{
     "The Stim export, ",
     Cell[BoxData["DEPOLARIZE1"], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "75c8f24b-f46e-7672-23f7-f414fd1b5d58"],
     " line for line against the model's slots"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"2d149507-d3df-875e-5b2b-0d60e66beda4"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "772d62ae-4bf9-dab0-1ed3-7b086d8da89a"], Cell[
    "Cat states", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "7a8c9a4d-0caa-515e-2ab3-1c17a55f23a4"], Cell["\<\
Every single fault propagated through the preparation, against the check set\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"6a4c6a75-6554-e0e6-1a73-8c3f0ce6b2cc"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "29c3108e-8c9d-f317-5ff0-89e82529de7d"], Cell[
    "The encoded ancillas", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "5b90d741-2df1-4c37-09af-cf2b4b84171d"], Cell[
    "The engine: $", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "5a353f88-1ea4-a3d5-0bca-b6d29b56f13f"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "3c3a5085-d835-7232-65da-49eed9c04118"], Cell[
    "Fault tolerance of the gadgets", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "2f71b61d-3801-a1b0-550e-2847b9b5f39a"], Cell["\<\
The residual data weight over every single fault, against the bare-ancilla \
circuit measuring the same operator\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"3c7c9f19-7bfc-9bea-6403-17437d8ee930"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "4bcd3c0f-0044-41be-79f2-b669b1f11384"], Cell["\<\
That a transversal extraction can go in a detector model at all\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"250574e2-7568-dee6-533b-6dcc7c02a4cc"], 
    Cell["\<\
Its effect on 200 random fault pairs, against the XOR of their rows\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"570dea5b-028b-2dc3-7d32-0c05b73e7729"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "559114f0-95cd-3728-03ae-8dba1c799a72"], Cell[
    "That it restores the exponent", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "499d2cc9-9173-f7c8-7fa2-c5932007dd12"], Cell["\<\
The rate at two physical rates a factor of two apart, slope read off\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"1b3687b6-15a3-de20-4acd-1ef09c57a50a"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "073f26db-34e5-c8c2-2ec4-bf85bc919a28"], Cell[
    "That a transversal CNOT is the logical CNOT", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "27056d96-6b3e-545a-4d3a-84d00ecb3ea0"], Cell["\<\
Conjugating the logical operators through it, and the stabilizer group \
mapping to itself\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"031df9cf-6b45-d275-3122-f0a90ef1a15f"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "79902eb9-9fc4-d4aa-2faf-c7e31a76bef0"], Cell[
    "That a transversal gate is the gate you think it is", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"6e90dac8-e749-9c1a-16af-d39592fde760"], Cell[TextData[{
     "The gate's own matrix, conjugated with the ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["Z",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "2f026f1c-d8c2-1814-5531-8759d9776b7e"],
     " phase carried; the logical gate against the complex conjugate of the \
physical one"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"5c65fa9b-46f3-ebf0-041a-f3c57287b9da"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "583cd303-9cb1-03ae-09c3-cb6d154451f4"], Cell[
    "That the assembled FT(C) computes C", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "18f1bad1-a8d9-f26a-488e-339ac96dc0b0"], Cell["\<\
The engine: the gate gadgets alone, run with no faults, must leave the blocks \
in the state the ideal circuit would\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"6cd8e50a-7117-62ea-14e7-fd5400a23030"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "7b9c4f1f-9707-8ca1-29a4-675922b3d68b"], Cell[
    "The exported circuit", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "0839f778-d15e-09ff-39c6-ef25e0eb5bc5"], Cell[
    "PyMatching, which decodes it unchanged", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "7962e333-0c57-77b8-2f11-fb7da5e25d82"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "0e58b71a-bb3b-e382-3667-2f443ecfb1e8"], Cell[
    "The encoder and codewords", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "7517e465-645e-477c-232c-fe4f0deb2a46"], Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
        StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], 
      "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "560e68d9-da1a-2272-7e35-8182dfaf7158"],
     ", ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
      "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "46aa8ea3-37c3-4040-6ea9-270d427612aa"],
     " against ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{"\[Product]", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", "+", 
          StyleBox["g", "TI"]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], 
      "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "6acb7fb5-f6da-6094-1ac9-76fe836f32fe"],
     ", and ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["P", "TI"], "_"], 
        StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
        StyleBox["P", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "7a5ec95d-e220-f105-2a65-e10697dac06f"],
     " for the code's own logical operators"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"05590d03-2064-1772-3366-a56d51117a58"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "3b9b9f37-eb8f-88a6-69b8-17708e3bda8c"], Cell[
    "The logical channel", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "7ef0eca9-2ea7-fc5e-268f-05f34b53c6a4"], Cell["\<\
The exact logical error rate, identically, and its action on a state against \
its own weights\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"53b0040e-15e9-970f-014f-9e68a39dfa55"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "49c5479d-c9fe-ab26-7ffb-5ec6ef88f60c"], Cell[
    "Knill\[Dash]Laflamme, symplectically", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "73b5640c-4acf-57ea-214b-7e566f7a3d30"], Cell[
    "Its dense definition over the codewords", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "12e31b8a-6cd9-3185-4290-92d4056d83ef"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "1c8dfb5f-95aa-8549-44b2-f3191c5cef93"], Cell[
    "Noise read from a channel", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "77ba1ed5-dc9c-5ed1-1d59-979ed529243b"], Cell["\<\
The channel's superoperator, and the named channels' known weights\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"122b6086-f39f-774a-4229-79e3862a5d90"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "562fd52b-4ccb-95a8-7fd4-cd75657ffff2"], Cell[
    "A decoder object", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6a176158-c8f1-b5ca-1a2d-7905e8851f10"], Cell["\<\
The engine's own decoding table, entry for entry, herald filter included\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"59294b9d-2c6b-0af3-08d7-62c7451e58d9"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "4c93342e-976f-2690-74a0-ad88221b8cfa"], Cell[
    "The retired names", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "0c05a0c6-8ada-cee6-343a-39a02f6c94cc"], Cell[
    "The value each returned before, and one warning per session", 
     "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"386c40c3-2c7c-2bd7-6814-59ad4509793d"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "38a5d185-6c33-4099-685a-c8ef05c612e3"], Cell[
    "The dual weight enumerator", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "705b2160-d6f6-9bc7-2078-b94de280e92d"], Cell["\<\
The normalizer enumerated directly, and the distance it implies (Thm 7.7)\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"3ad5a48d-d13d-ee7b-6aea-3dd6e0c9b541"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "3e286ad4-f19d-13f8-67d7-8391802861c2"], Cell[
    "The code-space probability", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "40ae3c14-0aab-252d-7055-b65eaf5f8c77"], Cell[TextData[{
     "The dense projector: ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "6"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "3710829e-7f3a-eae8-5d2f-1bd87accb832"],
     " on five copies of $"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"514f46f4-7214-5441-0775-5fbe07a13eab"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "5a8341fe-fd5d-b2cd-0ab1-58bbf4e90017"], Cell[
    "The Clifford hierarchy level", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "4cf942e0-12f7-a17b-7487-5bcaa683f041"], Cell[TextData[{
     "The book's own placements: ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       StyleBox["T", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "4db09b50-0334-b760-7b4f-131ab6c61a4a"],
     ", Toffoli, CCZ, ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       StyleBox[
        RowBox[{"C", "S"}], "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "7cb56032-9c81-172f-244b-7a7c15347a75"],
     " at 3, and one level per halving of the angle"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"55f15dca-bfed-9606-038f-54943999fd6c"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "5589ad74-704a-26e9-03b6-453e01fc8c33"], Cell[
    "The pseudothreshold", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "37fda5d4-10fa-7e26-5d82-3c9ea08f450c"], Cell[TextData[{
     "The binomial tail of the repetition code, which crosses at exactly ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "6cc64ef1-7b65-373d-14fe-67bb7e119a07"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"542582fc-1c6f-cfd5-7dda-1ba6951b953f"]}
  }]], "2ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"7ad84463-32de-d6a2-2af8-5e4d4768bc88"],

Cell["\<\
The habit is worth keeping when extending the layer: a result checked only \
against the code that produced it is not checked.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3261459d-f728-27c9-621f-5cc682c28d13"],

